# STEPWIRE environment
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for local development. NEVER commit a real value:
# `.env*` is git-ignored, and secrets used by automation belong in GitHub
# Secrets or Vercel Environment Variables, not in the repository.
#
# Nothing here is required to run the website. The site, the collector's
# fixture sources, the studio preview and local video rendering all work with
# no configuration at all.


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Site
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Canonical origin, used for metadata, canonicals, sitemap and RSS.
# On Vercel this is derived automatically from VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL;
# set it only for a custom domain.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://stepwire.example

# Set to `false` in production to exclude the seeded sample articles from the
# build entirely. Fixtures are already excluded from the RSS feed, the sitemap
# and search indexing, and are labelled in the UI.
# STEPWIRE_INCLUDE_FIXTURES=true


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# News collection  (GitHub Actions; not needed locally for --dry-run)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# A token with `issues: write` on this repository. In GitHub Actions the
# built-in `secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN` is used and nothing needs configuring; set
# this only to run `pnpm news:collect --create-issues` from your own machine.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=

# owner/repo. Provided automatically inside Actions.
# GITHUB_REPOSITORY=shunta-furukawa/stepwire


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Video rendering
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# REQUIRED for /api/render. Without it the endpoint is disabled and returns
# 503 — rendering fails closed rather than leaving a billable endpoint open.
# Generate one with: openssl rand -hex 32
# STEPWIRE_RENDER_TOKEN=

# Maximum renders per hour per instance. Defaults to 10.
# STEPWIRE_RENDER_RATE_LIMIT=10

# Force a render driver. Omit to choose automatically: `sandbox` when the
# Vercel credentials below are all present, `local` otherwise.
#   local   — runs Remotion in this process. No cost. Used by `pnpm video:render`.
#   sandbox — runs the render on a Vercel Sandbox machine.
# STEPWIRE_RENDER_DRIVER=

# Vercel Sandbox credentials. All three are required for cloud rendering.
#   VERCEL_TOKEN       Account settings → Tokens
#   VERCEL_TEAM_ID     Team settings → General
#   VERCEL_PROJECT_ID  Project settings → General
# VERCEL_TOKEN=
# VERCEL_TEAM_ID=
# VERCEL_PROJECT_ID=

# The repository the sandbox clones to perform the render. Defaults to this
# project's public GitHub URL; override for a fork or a private mirror.
# STEPWIRE_RENDER_REPO_URL=https://github.com/shunta-furukawa/stepwire.git

# The revision to render at. Defaults to the deployed commit
# (VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA), so a video always matches the article and design
# that were live when it was requested.
# STEPWIRE_RENDER_REVISION=

# Vercel Blob, where finished renders are stored. Created automatically when
# you add a Blob store to the project; also the authoritative duplicate check,
# so without it every render request starts a new render.
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=
